  "module_docs": [
    "Port of `net.minestom.server.network.packet.client.play.ClientPlayerActionPacket`.",
    "",
    "The `blockFace` is `BYTE.transform(aByte -> BlockFace.values()[aByte], face",
    "-> (byte) face.ordinal())` in Java \u2014 a raw signed byte, not a `VAR_INT` enum",
    "\u2014 and the `Status` is a `NetworkBuffer.Enum` (`VAR_INT` of the ordinal).",
    "[`BlockFace`] is reused from the sibling block-placement packet (a local",
    "stand-in for the `instance.block` enum)."
  ],
  "struct": {
    "docs": [
      "Java: `record ClientPlayerActionPacket(Status status, Point blockPosition,",
      "BlockFace blockFace, int sequence) implements ClientPacket.Play`.",
      "",
      "`Eq` is not derived: `block_position` is a float-backed [`Vec`], which is",
      "only `PartialEq` (Java's record `equals` compares the `double` components",
      "with `Double.compare`, so `-0.0 != 0.0` and `NaN == NaN` \u2014 semantics a",
      "derived Rust `Eq` cannot express)."
